Package: stim2-render
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: SheinbergLab
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: stim2 (>= @MIN_STIM2@), dlsh-interp, ffmpeg, init-system-helpers
Description: stim2 trial clips for dserv's trial viewer
 Installing this package turns on the stim2-render service: a headless
 stim2 that re-renders recorded trials frame-locked, as video clips for
 dserv's trial viewer (dg_viewer), on port 8140. It pauses while this
 machine's dserv runs an experiment. Removing the package turns it off.
 .
 The unit and the render server ship with stim2; this package is the
 switch, its settings (/etc/default/stim2-render), and what the server
 needs to run (the dlsh interpreter and ffmpeg).
